[{:db/id "q-9623/selection/f5b1cb523b8dbc8f19f048054a1644debbd863187b8a117a4110398194eeffb0" :answer/id #uuid "a3d34c65-1180-532f-bd46-bc08e5eab51b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\pi }≈1.773\\,9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-9623/selection/e6cef2ef0367aa7c28b778b36ef6d1e38165f0aad5dfbb7d474ef0bbe78acdaa" :answer/id #uuid "8beb57a2-9a93-5617-8158-fbe8681cc374" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\pi }≈1.732\\,2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-9623/selection/7a752d7479e57a0ec24a6da64dcd30785490ba8fe55b0c4a263ed066527e60e4" :answer/id #uuid "a496d11a-3260-56c7-b8cc-a7b01df5f213" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\pi }≈1.764\\,9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-9623/selection/7628b12ad1c50d7a02fd1d83874f46fd46df740d6307db291fcb73119e2611c2" :answer/id #uuid "66c0c571-c530-53f8-84be-f381739b9e19" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\pi }≈1.792\\,7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-9623/selection/c729ba725aab0303c7a4b236dec1bd3fb5096bc99f85d03e7182d0b1dbce7a97" :answer/id #uuid "c73e0d91-6e95-53f3-a811-152fe40e0643" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\pi }≈1.787\\,7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-9623/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f7cd1b69-97b5-50fb-bf77-12efcb36b6cc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-9623/selection/f5b1cb523b8dbc8f19f048054a1644debbd863187b8a117a4110398194eeffb0" :answer-field/choices ["q-9623/selection/f5b1cb523b8dbc8f19f048054a1644debbd863187b8a117a4110398194eeffb0" "q-9623/selection/e6cef2ef0367aa7c28b778b36ef6d1e38165f0aad5dfbb7d474ef0bbe78acdaa" "q-9623/selection/7a752d7479e57a0ec24a6da64dcd30785490ba8fe55b0c4a263ed066527e60e4" "q-9623/selection/7628b12ad1c50d7a02fd1d83874f46fd46df740d6307db291fcb73119e2611c2" "q-9623/selection/c729ba725aab0303c7a4b236dec1bd3fb5096bc99f85d03e7182d0b1dbce7a97"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-9623" :question/id #uuid "43923f1d-dfe1-5ab3-936a-6fc1d8791c67" :question/math-academy-id "q-9623" :question/problem "Use the first three non-zero terms of the Taylor expansion of $\\sqrt{x}$ about $x=4$ to approximate the value of $\\sqrt{\\pi }.$ Give your answer to $4$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "We use Taylor's formula in the form\n\n$$\nf(x)=f(a)+{f}^{′}(a)(x-a)+\\frac{{f}^{″}(a)}{2!}(x-a)^{2}+⋯,\n$$\n\nwith $a=4.$ \n\nCalculating the necessary derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\sqrt{x}={x}^{1/2} \\\\ f(4) & ={4}^{1/2}=2 \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{-1/2} \\\\ {f}^{′}(4) & =\\frac{1}{2}(4)^{-1/2}=\\frac{1}{{2}^{2}} \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =\\frac{1}{2}(-\\frac{1}{2}){x}^{-3/2}=-\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{-3/2} \\\\ {f}^{″}(4) & =-\\frac{1}{4}(4)^{-3/2}=-\\frac{1}{{2}^{5}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the Taylor series is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{x} & =2+\\frac{1}{{2}^{2}}(x-4)-\\frac{1}{2!}(\\frac{1}{{2}^{5}})(x-4)^{2}+⋯ \\\\  & =2+\\frac{x-4}{4}-\\frac{(x-4)^{2}}{64}+⋯\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute $x=\\pi $ into the above to approximate $\\sqrt{\\pi }.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{\\pi } & ≈2+\\frac{\\pi -4}{4}-\\frac{(\\pi -4)^{2}}{64} \\\\  & =1.773\\,9\\,,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nto $4$ decimal places." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-9623/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a239976c-cf11-5c26-b250-2c03b3fb1ec3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-9623"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-347637/field-1/2ee2cfe615154a44ab76e3add27527ea3aeb13df80b2aae862a301a9198678ea" :answer/id #uuid "aa61e374-3a73-5b17-9eb5-3eae45f312c9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1.02" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-347637/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "dae3ef6e-ab2e-5ade-ad19-cd3a59e37fff" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-347637/field-1/2ee2cfe615154a44ab76e3add27527ea3aeb13df80b2aae862a301a9198678ea" :answer-field/choices ["q-347637/field-1/2ee2cfe615154a44ab76e3add27527ea3aeb13df80b2aae862a301a9198678ea"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-347637" :question/id #uuid "9070d2fc-ef35-5217-a380-97c0b5a05359" :question/math-academy-id "q-347637" :question/problem "Use the first two non-zero terms of the Taylor expansion of $\\operatorname{sec}⁡x$ about $x=\\pi $ to approximate the value of $\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\pi +0.2).$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\pi +0.2)≈$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We use Taylor's formula in the form\n\n$$\nf(x)=f(a)+{f}^{′}(a)(x-a)+\\frac{{f}^{″}(a)}{2!}(x-a)^{2}+⋯,\n$$\n\nwith $f(x)=\\operatorname{sec}⁡x$ and $a=\\pi .$ \n\nCalculating the necessary derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡x \\\\ f(\\pi ) & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\pi )=-1 \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x \\\\ {f}^{′}(\\pi ) & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\pi )\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\pi )=0 \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡x{tan}^{2}⁡x+{sec}^{3}⁡x \\\\ {f}^{″}(\\pi ) & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\pi ){tan}^{2}⁡(\\pi )+{sec}^{3}⁡(\\pi )=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the Taylor series is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sec}⁡x & =-1+(0)(x-\\pi )+\\frac{(-1)}{2!}(x-\\pi )^{2}+⋯ \\\\  & =-1-\\frac{1}{2}(x-\\pi )^{2}+⋯.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute $x=\\pi +0.2$ into the above to approximate $\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\pi +0.2).$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\pi +0.2) & ≈-1-\\frac{1}{2}{(\\pi +0.2-\\pi )}^{2} \\\\  & =-1-\\frac{1}{2}(0.2)^{2} \\\\  & =-1-\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{1}{25}) \\\\  & =-1-\\frac{1}{50} \\\\  & =-\\frac{51}{50}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-347637/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a239976c-cf11-5c26-b250-2c03b3fb1ec3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-347637"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-353859/field-1/0d474ca756c76f6ecddcd5fcfb411f0292ef0ce725af778ee27af0d5dc8595bc" :answer/id #uuid "a09b2459-e7e0-5b55-a80a-e3ec777a3b87" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-e" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-353859/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "c2db4285-6cd5-5770-a25e-7d88e563f7f0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-353859/field-1/0d474ca756c76f6ecddcd5fcfb411f0292ef0ce725af778ee27af0d5dc8595bc" :answer-field/choices ["q-353859/field-1/0d474ca756c76f6ecddcd5fcfb411f0292ef0ce725af778ee27af0d5dc8595bc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-353859/field-2/a7dd68b7f3e97d6127467da82186a4108a35d2bd1ccee4169390308f6afb9f5d" :answer/id #uuid "7ffbebfb-f837-5e6c-b95e-3d4c9ef7df85" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{e}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-353859/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "8f8808fb-ebd6-5821-8758-222afaa6e475" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-353859/field-2/a7dd68b7f3e97d6127467da82186a4108a35d2bd1ccee4169390308f6afb9f5d" :answer-field/choices ["q-353859/field-2/a7dd68b7f3e97d6127467da82186a4108a35d2bd1ccee4169390308f6afb9f5d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-353859/field-3/21d9d9ed4ce616542edb555591f054a38ba8d1973844c96bc0f56fc9aaadb7da" :answer/id #uuid "b4289a5e-3f0c-59c8-b77d-091d5a143d3f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{e}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-353859/field-3" :answer-field/id #uuid "ecd3f18b-8e59-5ad0-bab0-fc4fce9c9fee" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-353859/field-3/21d9d9ed4ce616542edb555591f054a38ba8d1973844c96bc0f56fc9aaadb7da" :answer-field/choices ["q-353859/field-3/21d9d9ed4ce616542edb555591f054a38ba8d1973844c96bc0f56fc9aaadb7da"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-353859" :question/id #uuid "ab2ebb5a-5574-563b-a19e-a919adb7c6dc" :question/math-academy-id "q-353859" :question/problem "Find the first three non-zero terms of the Taylor expansion of $x{e}^{x+2}$ about $x=-1.$\n\n$x{e}^{x+2}=$ {{field-1}} $+\\,$\n{{field-2}}\n$(x+1)^{2}\\,+\\,$\n{{field-3}}\n$(x+1)^{3}+⋯$" :question/worked-solution "We use Taylor's theorem in the form\n\n$$\nf(x)=f(a)+{f}^{′}(a)(x-a)+\\frac{{f}^{″}(a)}{2!}(x-a)^{2}+\\frac{{f}^{‴}(a)}{3!}(x-a)^{3}+⋯,\n$$\n\nwith $f(x)=x{e}^{x+2}$ and $a=-1.$ \n\nComputing the required derivatives, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =x{e}^{x+2} \\\\ f(-1) & =(-1){e}^{1}=-e \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & ={e}^{x+2}+x{e}^{x+2}=(1+x){e}^{x+2} \\\\ {f}^{′}(-1) & =(1-1){e}^{1}=0 \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & ={e}^{x+2}+(1+x){e}^{x+2}=(2+x){e}^{x+2} \\\\ {f}^{″}(-1) & =(2-1){e}^{1}=e \\\\ {f}^{‴}(x) & ={e}^{x+2}+(2+x){e}^{x+2}=(3+x){e}^{x+2} \\\\ {f}^{‴}(-1) & =(3-1){e}^{1}=2e.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x{e}^{x+2} & =-e+(0)(x+1)+\\frac{e}{2!}(x+1)^{2}+\\frac{2e}{3!}(x+1)^{3}⋯ \\\\  & =-e+\\frac{e}{2}(x+1)^{2}+\\frac{e}{3}(x+1)^{3}⋯.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-353859/field-1" "q-353859/field-2" "q-353859/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e3146eb6-b4ef-554d-83c1-351a3fb15651"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-353859"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
